# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole checkout — including every
# `node_modules` in it, which for `examples/mobile` alone is most of a gigabyte
# sent to the daemon on every build. It is also a correctness matter, not only a
# speed one: `COPY packages packages` and `COPY dashboard dashboard` would
# otherwise carry a *host-built* `dist/` into the image, where it would be
# whatever was last compiled on somebody's laptop rather than what this build
# just produced.

.git
.github
**/node_modules

# Built on the host. The build stage compiles its own; shipping these would mean
# the image contains output nobody can trace to a commit.
dist
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed to build or run the server.
tests
conformance
examples
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Expo leftovers, if anyone has run the mobile example.
**/.expo
examples/mobile/android
examples/mobile/ios

# Never.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.togglekit
